  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "berklee-music-theory-book-1-p0045",
      "source_en": "Lesson 18. The Chromatic Scale\n\nA series of notes that move in a consistent direction, and begin and end on the same note, is called a scale. There are many kinds of scales. The chromatic scale moves by half steps up or down and can begin on any note. It has twelve notes. Listen to the chromatic scale on track 28. 28 The ascending chromatic scale uses sharps to help point in the upward direction of the scale.\n\nThe descending chromatic scale uses flats to point in the downward direction of the scale.",
